{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs5uFrSYbxmhyHsuYTze","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed both bugs in `sched/core.py`, and the test passes. I also ran a few cases around the March 29 DST change in Berlin. The results looked right, but I didn't add them as tests.\n\n**Root causes**\n1. **Skipped day after 22:00 UTC:** the function took the date from `now` in UTC (`now.date()`) instead of the date in `tz`. At 23:30 UTC it is already the next day in Berlin, so the candidate was built on the wrong day and a day was skipped.\n2. **Off by one hour at the DST change:** the \"advance one day\" step added 24 hours in UTC and converted back. A day that spans a DST change isn't 24 hours long in local time, so the result shifted by an hour.\n\n**Fix**\n- The candidate is now built from `now`'s date converted into `tz`.\n- If it isn't strictly after `now`, the loop moves to the next local calendar day with the same wall-clock time.\n- The candidate is round-tripped through UTC, so a time that doesn't exist because of the spring-forward gap lands on a real moment.\n\n**Checks (Berlin)**\n- 09:00 stays at 09:00 on both sides of the change: Mar 28 → Mar 29 09:00 +02:00, and Mar 29 → Mar 30 09:00 +02:00.\n- 02:30, which doesn't exist on Mar 29, comes out as 03:30 +02:00.\n\nThe signature is unchanged."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9395,"cache_read_input_tokens":31214,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9395},"output_tokens":478,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1ad7d0a9-60c9-4f9f-ba67-d68fb2577f62","uuid":"f766cb94-d85e-4882-b1a1-fa5a5056e765","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:49:28.854Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs5uFZaaH82vBYEq6QfX"}
